fa31b84c6ef6ddd3","intervals":[],"path":"test/workflows/action-pins.test.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Assert that `workflowdispatch` is the only trigger."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"c0004f100292fffe712e327c9df60ab916d3e547","body":"**Update the matrix for the armed gate.**\n\nThis paragraph says `gate.yml` runs without `--push` and `merge-queue-gate.yml` is the sole promoter. Both gate files now set `CQ_GATE_PROMOTES: 'true'`, and `docs/promotion-policy.md:107-118` says the legacy gate is retired. The matrix therefore gives operators the wrong promoter and check-enforcement model. Its phase instructions still direct changes to the retired gate (`docs/w4-obligation-matrix.md:351`). Mark this analysis as historical or revise the affected rollout instructions for the current gate.","id":"1f7f57405ee7970551e033a64f06901dcd2400bbb8729f9a09977dfc9052065e","intervals":[],"path":"docs/w4-obligation-matrix.md","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Update the matrix for the armed gate."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"a68f44bf5e979265e89ccda865e43db33d55a9f2","body":"**Align the ordinary-range selection contract.**\n\n`docs/promotion-policy.md:60-64` says an ordinary range is selected without signer success. However, `docs/promotion-policy.md:110-113` and `policy/templates/gate.yml:17-20,54-56` say the subject must carry trusted signer success and that no reviewed commit produces `awaiting`. These rules define different selection behavior.\n\nResolve the rule against `src/selfhost/promote-gate.ts`, then update the policy and gate template to match. Edit `policy/templates/gate.yml`, not the generated `.github/workflows/gate.yml`.","id":"78c74473c0c26bedfaeb9719bba59172baab7aa42ed3276549514aa09542f7f0","intervals":[],"path":"docs/promotion-policy.md","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Align the ordinary-range selection contract."}],"head":"d2302ff14f866462adcf6